  "worked_solution": "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$ \n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/72f59260e2d8e20a163fb4462a6332c4fafd00078a6e851806b30b9c005a0ae3.png)\n\nNote that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/72aac3f5d5f3b58e571df5c2b8d35523af379dabf66b40c3018eba573b119fca.png)",
